<name>Wireless Door Lock Control System</name>
<para id="RM0000005BB010X" category="C" type-id="300UQ" name-id="622PB-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1242</dtccode>
<dtcname>Wireless tuner system malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005BB010X_04" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002CE00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The door control receiver (smart receiver) receives the signal from the electrical key transmitter and sends it via the smart key computer assembly (certification ECU) to the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) by multiplex communication. The instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) controls the door locks by sending door lock and door unlock signals to each door lock actuator.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The wireless door lock control system has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When using SST (TaSCAN) with the ignition switch OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON←→OFF until communication between SST (TaSCAN) and the vehicle starts. (ON←→OFF interval within 1.5 seconds)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the electrical key transmitter or smart key computer assembly (certification ECU) has been replaced, refer to the registration procedure in the immobiliser reference section.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Check that there are no other electrical key transmitters in the vehicle interior.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.85in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.33in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.90in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
